  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>College of San Mateo is a public community college in San Mateo, California. Located in the northern corridor of Silicon Valley, the University has been a gateway to higher education since 1922.</p><p>CSM offers various programs, including traditional, semester-length, and short courses and distance education. The 153-acre site is situated idyllically in the San Mateo hills, providing a stunning view of the famous San Francisco Bay. Approximately 325 international students from different nationalities attend the University each year, making the campus a hive of multiple cultures.</p><p>The Health &amp; Wellness Center gives students health services, including medical care, counseling, and wellness coaching.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>The College of San Mateo does not provide accommodation options, but the student life section of the website has resources to help international students specifically find suitable housing options during their time at the University. Students can find listings of apartments and hotels in the nearby area via the University website. Many international students opt to live in a homestay program to advance their grasp of the English language and feel seamlessly integrated into the culture.</p><p>If students have friends attending the same University, they often cut costs and boost their social life by sharing with roommates.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Sports",
      "value": "<p>Fitness is a big part of many students lives. The gymnasium includes a full-size basketball court and weight training room for sporty students. Tennis courts, soccer, and softball fields, and a track and field complex can also be accessed throughout the campus.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Lab",
      "value": "<p>Specialized learning is empowered via spaces such as the Science Building and Creative Arts Building, where facilities such as science labs, a theater, and more amenities are available.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Library",
      "value": "<p>The library offers a range of resources, including books and online databases. The Learning Resource Center is the leading academic support center on campus, where students can access study skills workshops, tutoring, academic counseling, and more resources.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student Life",
      "value": "<p>Students are well-supported to enjoy their time at this inclusive campus. The Center for Student Life is where a responsive team works hard to resolve student inquiries and provide as much assistance as possible. Cultural activities and events occur regularly where students can learn from leaders in their academic field, be entertained by live music or network with past alums. There are over 30 student clubs at the College of San Mateo for students to enjoy various activities.</p><p>The Center for Student Life and Leadership Development was implemented to help students who want to continually develop their employability skills and put themselves in the best position to reach the highest qualification. The Campus Life Leadership Awards recognize particularly active students and there are other initiatives for students to get involved with the local community via volunteer work.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
